:translit "bet b'masrah", :gloss "two times in the Masorah"} {:he "וחדל לעולם", :translit "v'chadal la-olam", :gloss "and neglects forever"} {:he "דפסח בכרת", :translit "da-pesach b'karet", :gloss "for Passover is in karet"} {:he "וחדל לעולם לעולמו של יובל דהיינו חמשים שנה", :translit "v'chadal la-olam l'olamo shel yovel da-heinu chamishim shanah", :gloss "and neglects forever means for the lifetime of the jubilee, that is, fifty years"} {:he "כדין חייבי כריתות דלא מפקי חמשים", :translit "ka-dein chayavei k'ritot da-lo mafkei chamishim", :gloss "like the law of those liable to karet who do not go out beyond fifty"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וחדל" "וחדל לעולם"]}], :frame {:text "The punishment of karet is understood as premature death at the hand of Heaven. The school of Rabbi Ishmael derives from the verse 'that soul shall be utterly cut off' (Numbers 15:31) that karet means dying before age sixty. An additional baraita attributed to Resh Lakish states that those liable to karet do not live past fifty, deriving this from the jubilee cycle counted as fifty years (Leviticus 25:10). The Gemara cites this as 'the school of Eliyahu: anyone liable to karet does not live past fifty years' (Mo'ed Katan 28a).", :sources ["Numbers 15:31" "Leviticus 25:10" "Mo'ed Katan 28a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ונכרתה הנפש ההוא", :translit "ve-nichr'tah ha-nefesh ha-hu", :gloss "and that soul shall be cut off"} {:he "ס\" ת אשה", :translit "sofei tevot ishah", :gloss "final letters spell woman"} {:he "אחד האיש ואחד האשה בכלל עונשין", :translit "echad ha-ish ve-echad ha-ishah b'cholal onshin", :gloss "both a man and a woman are included in punishments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ונכרתה הנפש ההוא", :spells "אשה"}], :frame {:text "The principle that women are included in the punishment of karet for neglecting the Paschal offering is established by the hermeneutic of comparison. Since the verses for Paschal neglect (Numbers 9:13) and for karet from the New Moon passage (Numbers 15:31) use parallel language of 'that soul,' the gender-neutral term 'nefesh' is read as encompassing both men and women in the domain of punishments, just as the Talmud derives from comparable parallels (Keritot 3b).", :sources ["Numbers 9:13" "Numbers 15:31" "Keritot 3b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ובדרך" "וילך בדרך אביו" "ובדרך אמו" "ובדרך ירבעם בן נבט" "ובדרך חטאים לא עמד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ובדרך", :refs ["Numbers 9:13" "1 Kings 22:53" "Jeremiah 6:25" "Psalms 1:1"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וילך בדרך אביו", :refs ["1 Kings 15:26" "1 Kings 22:53" "2 Chronicles 20:32"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ובדרך אמו", :refs ["1 Kings 22:53"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ובדרך ירבעם בן נבט", :refs ["1 Kings 22:53"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ובדרך חטאים לא עמד", :refs ["Psalms 1:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וחדל" "וחדל לעולם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וחדל", :refs ["Numbers 9:13" "Isaiah 53:3" "Psalms 49:9"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וחדל לעולם", :refs ["Psalms 49:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ונכרתה הנפש ההוא", :spells "אשה", :letters ["ה" "ש" "א"], :by :selah, :order :bag}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:13.981005153Z", :model "glm-5.2"}